@@ -396,6 +396,7 @@ Note 2: Master–vassal(s) changes are intended to strengthen overall AI play by
 - Disable unreliable **UnitAIs** for AIs: `UNITAI_COLLATERAL`, `UNITAI_PILLAGE` (but despite that, AI still seems to occasionally pillage), `UNITAI_PIRATE_SEA` to reduce suicides/baiting and keep stacks focused.
 - Retune UnitAI **selection/weights** in `AI_bestUnit`, `AI_bestUnitAI`, `AI_chooseProduction`: land maps emphasize `UNITAI_ATTACK` / `UNITAI_ATTACK_CITY` (with some `UNITAI_RESERVE`); defense mode emphasizes `UNITAI_CITY_DEFENSE` / `UNITAI_CITY_SPECIAL` / `UNITAI_RESERVE`; naval UnitAIs are downweighted on land-focused maps. Goal: fewer wandering/baited units; more decisive stacks.
 - (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 6087+) **AI military production now catches up when an empire becomes under-strength for its size:** dedicated BBAI military-production logging together with SASGameRecord exposed a Base AdvCiv/K-Mod asymmetry: relative-power logic could reduce unit production when an AI was already strong, but there was no opposite catch-up when expansion outpaced army growth. This could leave a rapidly expanding empire with too little military for the amount of territory and cities it needed to defend. To address this, the AI now compares its power per city with the city-weighted average of relevant rivals and proportionally increases its normal willingness to build units while under-strength, while still respecting financial/economic reductions, the better-units strategy and the inherited high-power throttle. In two full post-fix runs from save file 458 and an independent post-fix run from save file 457, this catch-up activated in about 46-47% of logged military-production evaluations when applicable. For example, one save-file 458 state had Kublai at 9 cities and 579 power (about 64 power per city versus 125 for the relevant-rival average), increasing his BuildUnitProb from 47 to 70; save file 457 independently showed Shaka at 7 cities and 377 power (about 54 versus 94 per city), increasing it from 57 to 81. In practice, under-strength AIs therefore became noticeably more willing to reinforce their armies until they caught up, while already-strong AIs received no boost. See [KI#197](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#197---fixedimproved-base-advcivk-mod-military-production-could-remain-too-low-when-an-empire-was-under-strength-for-its-size-because-relative-power-logic-only-throttled-strong-ais).
+- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 6088+) **The AI's final important-building retry now respects military-production pressure while another unit still fits its spending budget:** military-production logs showed that Base AdvCiv/K-Mod could reach the end of city production with strong reasons to build units, then give an important building one final chance that ignored that military pressure: in `CvCityAI::AI_chooseProduction`, short-circuit 2 already lowers building odds as `iBuildUnitProb` rises, but short-circuit 3 - the final "last chance to catch important buildings" immediately before generic unit production - recalculated its building chance from building value and land-war state alone. Strong military-production pressure could therefore survive the earlier production logic and then be partly forgotten at the final building retry. In the severe under-strength samples that exposed the issue, this late building retry won 7/9 and 7/8 times in two save-file 458 runs and 15/25 times in save file 457. To fix this, the AI now reduces only this final building chance in proportion to its existing willingness to build units, and only while the normal military-spending gate still has room; once the AI is already over that unit budget, the inherited building odds are left unchanged. The final save-file 458 validation left 375/640 already-over-budget evaluations untouched, while severe under-strength cases that still had spending room fell from about 48% average base building odds to about 33% and chose the building only 5/25 times. This keeps important infrastructure possible while preventing the last building retry from disproportionately overriding the military pressure already used by the surrounding production logic. See [KI#197.2](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#1972---fixedimproved-base-advcivk-mod-final-building-short-circuit-cvcityaiai_chooseproductions-short-circuit-3-ignored-buildunitprob-and-could-override-strong-military-production-pressure-immediately-before-generic-unit-production).
 - Rebalance perceived **iPower**: downweight some naval units; adjust certain land units (e.g., warrior, animals) to reduce **fake power** that triggers bad wars. See [Long_Comments/Long_Comments_XML.txt](/Long_Comments/Long_Comments_XML.txt) (search for `UnitAI notes (Units XML)`).
 - XML **DefaultUnitAI / UnitAIs / NotUnitAIs**: align roles with efficiency (e.g., swordsmen primarily offensive even if versatile; longbows defensive unless explicitly set otherwise).
 - Promotions logic in `CvUnitAI::AI_promotionValue`: add **hard rules** so AIs pick context-appropriate promotions (e.g., City Garrison for `UNITAI_CITY_DEFENSE`, City Raider for `UNITAI_ATTACK_CITY`; avoid Woodsman/Medic on front-line attackers unless context justifies). Rules apply per **UnitAI** (not just by unit type); with exceptions like recon. See **[KI#47](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#47---fixed--addressed--enhanced-ai-choosing-poorly-promotions-for-its-units-now-added-a-set-of-hard-rules-in-which-case-some-promotions-are-not-good-and-to-ignore-as-is-most-efificient-in-most-times-and-rarely-cases-where-some-promotions-are-best-to-always-go-first-for-eg-as-of-no-city_garrison-first-for-unitai_city_defense-city_raider-first-for-unitai_attack_city-etc-if-any-more)**.

